# C048 — @suluk/payments: provider-agnostic payments, a Workers-native TS reimplementation of the Hyperswitch Prism
# connector interface. Operator: "use hyperswitch-prism mainly, implement it instead of a stripe broker + in billing,
# deprecate @suluk/stripe for a more agnostic solution" -> on the Workers-incompatibility finding: "if we cant run it,
# reimplement their interfaces to stay agnostic + switch providers easily + stay light" -> chose "ADR + interface first".
# NOT a contract facet (app-runtime lib; never touches the matcher). Supersedes @suluk/billing's payment surface.

# THE LOAD-BEARING FINDING (researched, not assumed): Prism is a stateless UNIFIED connector library (one schema, 100+
# processors, switch by config) BUT its Node SDK is a NATIVE FFI ADDON (koffi -> connector-service-ffi.node -> Rust core;
# Node 18+, platform binaries). Cloudflare Workers (V8 isolates) FORBID native modules, and @suluk/billing is
# Workers-native -> billing CANNOT import hyperswitch-prism. Decision: adopt Prism's INTERFACE + integer-exact status
# semantics, REIMPLEMENT in TS over fetch (zero native deps, edge-safe, no sidecar) -> agnostic + light, and a real Prism
# backend stays swappable later. DESIGNED + interface built => ceiling 0.5.
claim payments_prism_interface_reimpl_workers_native_decision: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when payments_prism_interface_reimpl_workers_native_decision == False

# C048 INTERFACE BUILT 2026-07-01 (operator chose interface-first; implementations deferred). @suluk/payments: types.ts —
# the unified schema (AuthorizeRequest/PaymentResponse/capture/void/refund/sync, MinorAmount, PaymentMethod card|token,
# Secret<T> PCI-scope wrap) + PaymentStatus/RefundStatus as PRISM-INTEGER-EXACT enums (CHARGED=8, AUTHORIZED=6, VOIDED=11,
# FAILURE=21, AUTHENTICATION_PENDING=4, REFUND_SUCCESS=4, REFUND_PENDING=3) so a Prism backend drops in + connector
# semantics match; a soft decline is IN-BAND FAILURE never thrown. connector.ts — the PaymentConnector SEAM (core flows
# required; customer/tokenize/recurring/webhook optional per-connector) + the Prism-style paymentClient(config, registry)
# where the CONFIG names the processor (switch by config not code); connectors are fetch-based (HttpOptions.fetch mockable
# transport). errors.ts — IntegrationError/ConnectorError/NetworkError (Prism's hard-failure split). mock.ts — a mock
# connector proving the seam + a local/test stand-in (decline card->FAILURE, 3DS->AUTH_PENDING, auto/manual->CHARGED/
# AUTHORIZED, coherent capture/void/refund/sync). deps: ZERO (Workers-native). WITNESSED — payments 7 pass: integer-exact
# enums, config-selects-connector + zero/many/unknown IntegrationError guards, the full flow, in-band decline, 3DS
# redirection. tsc clean. DEFERRED (post-approval): real connectors (stripe first, then adyen/...); the @suluk/billing
# rewire behind @suluk/payments (parity-tested vs @suluk/stripe); the C047 payment-connector broker (THIN — the interface
# is stateless, so it validates/registers a connectorConfig, not Stripe products); the eventual @suluk/stripe deprecation
# (NOT touched yet — deprecating before the replacement is proven would strand the live money path).
claim payments_agnostic_interface_built_witnessed: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when payments_agnostic_interface_built_witnessed == False

# C048 BUILD #2 — the BUILT-IN STRIPE ADAPTER + the BILLING REWIRE built 2026-07-01 (operator: "add builtin stripe
# adapter and rewire billing"). connectors/stripe.ts: stripeConnector — the FIRST real backend, unified schema <-> Stripe
# REST over fetch (Workers-native, no stripe SDK, no native dep). The PARITY-CRITICAL part is the STATUS MAPPING (a wrong
# map silently mis-reports money): mapPiStatus (succeeded->CHARGED, requires_capture->AUTHORIZED, requires_action->
# AUTHENTICATION_PENDING+redirect, processing->PENDING, canceled->VOIDED, requires_payment_method->FAILURE) + mapRefund
# Status (succeeded->SUCCESS, pending->PENDING, failed/canceled->FAILURE). authorize (raw card OR saved token, confirm,
# off_session, capture_method, metadata + Idempotency-Key=auth:<merchantTxnId>), capture/void/refund/sync/createCustomer.
# SOFT declines IN-BAND: a 3DS authentication_required -> AUTHENTICATION_PENDING; an HTTP 402 (or type card_error) -> a
# card decline FAILURE; only a non-402 hard/transport error THROWS ConnectorError/NetworkError (Prism's contract).
# PaymentMethod.token flattened to a Secret; AuthorizeRequest gained offSession + metadata. BILLING REWIRE (billing deps
# += @suluk/payments): agnostic.ts (paymentConnector(cfg)=stripeConnector bound to the billing StripeConfig, swappable in
# ONE line; statusString maps the unified status back to billing's Stripe-ish strings). createCustomer (billing.ts) +
# chargeOffSession (payments.ts) NOW ROUTE THROUGH the connector — same off-session PI request (amount/currency/customer/
# payment_method/off_session/confirm + app metadata userId/credits/source), same {id,status,authRequired} return + decline
# taxonomy (3DS->authRequired, 402->returned-not-thrown, transport->throws); a fresh crypto.randomUUID() merchantTxnId
# preserves "every call is a new charge". The browser/Element/hosted-Checkout + subscription flows STAY direct (they need
# the client-token surface — the next migration). WITNESSED — payments 16 pass (the stripe request shape + EVERY status arm
# incl. in-band 402 decline + 3DS + throw-on-500), billing 32 pass (the EXISTING billing-v2 suite still green THROUGH the
# new innards = behavioural parity, + the new agnostic bridge). tsc clean both. @suluk/stripe still NOT deprecated (billing
# checkout/subscriptions/webhook still use it — the remaining call-by-call migration). REMAINING: migrate the browser/
# hosted/subscription flows (client-token surface) -> then flip default -> mark @suluk/stripe deprecated; more connectors
# (adyen/...); the C047 payment-connector broker.
claim payments_stripe_adapter_and_billing_rewire_built: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when payments_stripe_adapter_and_billing_rewire_built == False

# C048 BUILD #3 — the SWAP: billing off @suluk/stripe entirely, ONE Stripe client (2026-07-01, operator: "swap it, I dont
# want to accidentally use legacy"). FINDING: billing's ONLY @suluk/stripe import was `toForm` (transport.ts); the browser/
# checkout/subscription/tax/card ops are Stripe-PLATFORM ops with NO agnostic equivalent (Prism is stateless — no product/
# price/checkout/customer-PM management), so they can't be "made agnostic" — but they CAN ride ONE Stripe client instead
# of a separate legacy path. Moved the low-level Stripe transport into @suluk/payments/stripe-transport.ts (StripeConfig +
# stripePost/stripeGet byte-identical + an ARRAY-AWARE toForm handling checkout/subscription nested arrays line_items[0]
# [price_data][...]); the stripeConnector's call() now rides it (one transport impl). billing/transport.ts RE-EXPORTS from
# @suluk/payments; @suluk/stripe REMOVED from billing deps. Now billing has a SINGLE Stripe access point: agnostic FLOWS
# (createCustomer/chargeOffSession) via the connector, Stripe-PLATFORM ops via the same transport — no accidental second
# path. PARITY PROVEN: the full billing suite (32 pass, incl. every checkout/subscription form-encoding assertion
# %5B0%5D%5B...%5D) stays green through the swapped transport + array-aware toForm; payments 16 pass; tsc clean both.
# @suluk/stripe NOT blanket-deprecated (honest — still the ONLY impl for testgen's pricing-conformance primitives +
# the app's webhook signature verification), but its description now steers payment-flow work to @suluk/payments. REMAINING:
# port the pricing primitives + webhook-verify off @suluk/stripe (then retire it); the client-token surface for the
# browser-Element flows; more connectors (adyen/...).
claim payments_billing_swapped_single_stripe_client_no_legacy: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when payments_billing_swapped_single_stripe_client_no_legacy == False

# C048 BUILD #4 — retire @suluk/stripe to a SHIM: port pricing + webhook, repoint testgen (2026-07-01, operator: "do that
# update other packages like testgen and stripe"). MOVED into @suluk/payments (the payments+money home): pricing.ts
# (VERBATIM — the processor-agnostic checkout math: subtotal/orderTotal/composeTotal/verifyAmount anti-tamper/prorate
# Discount exact-sum/validateDiscount/idempotencyKey/cartFingerprint/requiresStripe/STRIPE_MIN_CHARGE_CENTS) + stripe-
# webhook.ts (verifyStripeSignature Web-Crypto HMAC + timingSafeHexEqual + webhookRouter + STRIPE_EVENTS; the webhook
# WebhookEvent renamed StripeWebhookEvent {type; data?} to avoid colliding with the connector's WebhookEvent). @suluk/
# payments stays ZERO-DEP (pricing pure, webhook Web-Crypto builtin). @suluk/stripe: pricing.ts + webhook-verify.ts +
# webhook.ts are now DEPRECATED RE-EXPORT SHIMS (`export ... from "@suluk/payments"`), so every existing @suluk/stripe
# import (incl. checkout.ts's internal `from ./pricing` + the app's webhook-verify) KEEPS WORKING; package.json gains the
# `deprecated` field + a @suluk/payments dep; the Stripe-specific unported bits (usage Billing-Meters, checkout params,
# shipping/tax adapters) remain frozen. testgen: generateMoneyTests default module -> "@suluk/payments" (+ provenance
# comments + its smoke test now imports the primitives from @suluk/payments); devDep @suluk/stripe -> @suluk/payments. NO
# dependency cycle (@suluk/payments zero-dep; @suluk/stripe -> @suluk/payments one-way). WITNESSED — payments 21 pass (+5:
# direct pricing anti-tamper/exact-prorate/idempotency + verifyStripeSignature valid/tampered/stale + router dispatch),
# stripe 71 pass (its full suite green THROUGH the shims = the move is behaviour-preserving), testgen 14 pass (smoke now
# runs against @suluk/payments), billing 32 pass. tsc clean all. REMAINING to fully delete @suluk/stripe: port the
# Stripe-usage-billing + checkout-params + shipping/tax (or drop if unused) + the app webhook cutover; the client-token
# surface for browser-Element flows; more connectors (adyen/...).
claim payments_stripe_retired_to_shim_pricing_webhook_ported_testgen_repointed: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when payments_stripe_retired_to_shim_pricing_webhook_ported_testgen_repointed == False

# C048 BUILD #5 — GUT @suluk/stripe to a deprecation shell, remove on next major (2026-07-01, operator: "gut it to
# deprecate it on major update"). VERIFIED SAFE FIRST: grep proved NOTHING in the workspace imports @suluk/stripe (billing
# swapped, testgen repointed), and the external app (toolfactory) imports ONLY verifyStripeSignature/webhookRouter/
# STRIPE_EVENTS/toForm — ALL of which now live in @suluk/payments. So the entire Stripe-specific remainder is DEAD
# everywhere. DELETED (894 LOC, 13 files): src/{stripe(usage Billing-Meters + @suluk/cost bridge),checkout,shipping,tax,
# rest(restStripe/retrievePaymentIntent),types(PaymentProvider/StripeLike)}.ts + their 4 tests + the now-redundant
# pricing/webhook/webhook-verify shim FILES. @suluk/stripe/src is now ONE index.ts = a DEPRECATION SHELL re-exporting from
# @suluk/payments (pricing + webhook verify/router + toForm/transport) so every surviving consumer (the app's 4 imports +
# the 2 kept tests) keeps working; @deprecated banner + package `deprecated` field say "removed in the next major".
# package.json dropped the @suluk/cost dep + the stripe SDK peerDep (both only the deleted code used them). WITNESSED —
# stripe 36 pass (pricing + webhook-verify survivor tests, now exercising @suluk/payments through the shell), payments 21,
# testgen 14, billing 32; tsc clean all; a runtime probe confirms the app's 4 exports resolve from the gutted index. @suluk/
# stripe: 836 LOC/10 files -> ~30-line shell. REMAINING: the client-token surface (browser-Element flows) + more connectors
# (adyen/...) + the eventual major-version DELETION of @suluk/stripe (after the app drops even the shim).
claim payments_stripe_gutted_to_deprecation_shell_remove_on_major: Bool @>=0.62 = True
falsified_when payments_stripe_gutted_to_deprecation_shell_remove_on_major == False

# C048 BUILD #6 — the CLIENT-TOKEN SURFACE (Prism's MerchantAuthenticationClient analog) built 2026-07-01 (operator: "do
# the client-token surface"). The piece a pure server-side authorize CAN'T express: create a server-side intent, hand a
# CONFIRMABLE TOKEN to the browser (PCI-scope reduction — raw card never touches the server; credit lands on the webhook).
# @suluk/payments types: ClientSession {clientSecret, connectorTransactionId?, customerId?} + CreatePaymentSessionRequest
# (amount, customerId?, paymentMethod? saved-token=one-click | omit=Payment-Element, setupFutureUsage?, captureMethod?,
# metadata?) + CreateSetupSessionRequest {customerId, metadata?}. PaymentConnector gained OPTIONAL createPaymentSession? +
# createSetupSession?. stripeConnector impl: createPaymentSession -> POST /payment_intents (token -> payment_method +
# payment_method_types[card] one-click; else automatic_payment_methods; +setup_future_usage; NO confirm — the BROWSER
# confirms) -> client_secret; createSetupSession -> POST /setup_intents (usage=off_session) -> client_secret. BILLING
# REWIRE: the last direct-Stripe PAYMENT-FLOW funcs now route through it — createPaymentIntent (Element) + createSetupIntent
# (add-card) [billing.ts] + createPaymentIntentOnDefaultCard (one-click, resolves default PM then pins) [payments.ts];
# same Stripe requests + client-secret returns + null-when-no-card. WITNESSED — payments 25 pass (+4: Element auto-PM +
# save + no-confirm, one-click pinned no-auto-PM, setup usage=off_session, throw-on-no-secret), billing 32 (existing
# setup-intent + one-click tests green THROUGH the new innards = parity). tsc clean. Payment FLOWS are now FULLY agnostic
# (charge/refund/customer + browser-confirmable sessions). What stays on the transport (NOT legacy — @suluk/payments' one
# client): the genuinely Stripe-PLATFORM ops with no agnostic equivalent — saved-card list/set-default/detach, hosted
# Checkout/portal, subscription CRUD, Stripe Tax. REMAINING: more connectors (adyen/...); the eventual @suluk/stripe
# major-version deletion.
claim payments_client_token_surface_built_billing_element_flows_agnostic: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when payments_client_token_surface_built_billing_element_flows_agnostic == False
